WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.124 --> 00:00:09.818
Ally couldn't bear the thought of upsetting Ray with Alpha's constant squawking.

2
00:00:09.819 --> 00:00:16.719
He had given her so much—a job, delicious meals, a place to live.

3
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:28.740
"I have to move," she told herself. "I can't stay here much longer."

4
00:00:28.741 --> 00:00:34.543
She spent the whole week looking for a place that she could afford.

5
00:00:34.544 --> 00:00:38.484
She finally found a room to rent in a boardinghouse.

6
00:00:38.485 --> 00:00:43.279
"I'll take it," Ally said to the landlord. "When can I move in?"

7
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.669
"Now, as long as you pay the first month's rent and—"

8
00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:50.022
Ram-bam-bop-boop! Loud music interrupted the landlord.

9
00:00:50.023 --> 00:00:54.359
She cupped her hands over her ears. "What's that awful noise?"

10
00:00:54.360 --> 00:01:00.565
"I'm sorry. It's just my device." Ally fumbled, trying to turn the volume down on the device.

11
00:01:00.566 --> 00:01:04.112
"It's not working very well, and it does this sometimes."

12
00:01:04.113 --> 00:01:09.496
"Well, then you can forget about renting this room!" the landlord fumed.

13
00:01:09.497 --> 00:01:13.699
"This is a quiet house. We don't allow loud music."

14
00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:17.217
"It's not what you think," Ally said.

15
00:01:17.218 --> 00:01:23.781
But the landlord led her to the front door and slammed it behind her.

16
00:01:23.782 --> 00:01:27.113
Out on the street, Ally pulled Alpha out of her pocket.

17
00:01:27.114 --> 00:01:33.553
"This is the third time you've blurted out noise and ruined our chances of renting a room!"

18
00:01:33.554 --> 00:01:38.646
"Apologies," Alpha said. "The device is scrambling Alpha's interface."

19
00:01:38.647 --> 00:01:42.671
Ally sighed. "It's all my fault.

20
00:01:42.672 --> 00:01:50.105
If I were a responsible Astralian, I would have cloaked the pod, and none of this would ever have happened."

21
00:01:50.106 --> 00:01:56.612
"Astralian wisdom says that mistakes are necessary to learning," Alpha said.

22
00:01:56.613 --> 00:01:59.324
"Thanks for saying that," Ally said.

23
00:01:59.325 --> 00:02:02.459
"But I'm not sure my parents would see it the same way.

24
00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:08.335
Anyway, just to be safe, I'd better power you down anytime we're around humans.

25
00:02:08.336 --> 00:02:13.903
Especially tonight—at the gala."

26
00:02:13.904 --> 00:02:21.469
*** When Ally arrived at the diner for the gala, Flo and Randy were busy setting

27
00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:26.279
up. They'd placed little vases shaped like rocket ships on the tables and hung up a giant

28
00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:31.049
sign: Welcome, League of Rocket

29
00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.897
Scientists! "It looks awesome in here!" Ally

30
00:02:34.898 --> 00:02:43.961
exclaimed. "You haven't seen the best part." Flo nudged Randy. "Show her what you

31
00:02:43.962 --> 00:02:48.350
made." Randy retrieved a tray from the

32
00:02:48.351 --> 00:02:54.105
kitchen. "It's nothing really. I was just having some

33
00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:56.344
fun." Ally looked at Randy's

34
00:02:56.345 --> 00:03:04.064
creations. "Wow, Randy! You've made meatballs look like planets and pastries look like telescopes and computers!"

35
00:03:04.065 --> 00:03:09.006
"Wait until you see the cake he made!" Flo said.

36
00:03:09.007 --> 00:03:15.487
"Not yet though," Randy said. "Let me put the finishing touches on it first."

37
00:03:15.488 --> 00:03:19.941
"I can't wait," Ally said. "I'll go wash my hands in the restroom.

38
00:03:19.942 --> 00:03:27.362
Then I'll help you finish preparing the food and decorations, Flo."

39
00:03:27.363 --> 00:03:31.214
By the time Ally returned to the dining room, Mateo had arrived.

40
00:03:31.215 --> 00:03:36.152
"I left gifts all over town for Bethany," he was explaining to Randy and Flo.

41
00:03:36.153 --> 00:03:41.116
"So far she's found an action figure and a pack of Cosmic Quest trading cards.

42
00:03:41.117 --> 00:03:45.824
Hopefully she's on her way to the comics bookstore for her next present and clue."

43
00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:50.000
"Where will the final clue lead her?" Flo asked.

44
00:03:50.001 --> 00:03:53.470
"To the red heart sculpture," Mateo replied.

45
00:03:53.471 --> 00:03:55.321
"That's where I'll give her the T-shirt.

46
00:03:55.322 --> 00:04:00.501
But after she figures out the clue at the bookshop, she'll come here to find the clue in the bathroom.

47
00:04:00.502 --> 00:04:06.938
I'd better get out of here! I don't want her to find me until the end."

48
00:04:06.939 --> 00:04:10.678
"Will you be back in time for the gala?" Ally asked.

49
00:04:10.679 --> 00:04:18.884
"I hope so!" Mateo hurried out the back door just as Bethany came in the front.

50
00:04:18.885 --> 00:04:27.171
"Oh, hi, Bethany!" Ally tried to act surprised to see Bethany. "What are you doing here?"

51
00:04:27.172 --> 00:04:34.425
"I'm on a scavenger hunt," Bethany replied in a flat voice. "A clue led me here."

52
00:04:34.426 --> 00:04:37.554
"What is it?" Ally asked.

53
00:04:37.555 --> 00:04:42.858
Bethany recited Mateo's riddle: "'Give me a tap and I'll give you some suds.

54
00:04:42.859 --> 00:04:45.856
I come in handy when you're covered in mud.'"

55
00:04:45.857 --> 00:04:50.365
Then she added sadly, "The answer is soap."

56
00:04:50.366 --> 00:04:56.028
Ally peered at her. "Are you okay?"

57
00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:59.143
Bethany shrugged and headed for the restroom.

58
00:04:59.144 --> 00:05:03.306
"Huh," Ally thought. "She seems upset."

59
00:05:03.307 --> 00:05:10.809
Ally did a quick scan of Bethany's mind. "Oh no!" Ally thought.

60
00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:18.725
"Bethany is upset about something—she thinks Mateo likes me! This is terrible!"

61
00:05:18.726 --> 00:05:20.192
Ally paced around.

62
00:05:20.193 --> 00:05:26.438
When Bethany came out, Ally had to find a way to reassure her that Mateo and Ally were just good friends.

63
00:05:26.439 --> 00:05:30.401
But before Bethany was back, Ray called Ally into the kitchen.

64
00:05:30.402 --> 00:05:42.123
And by the time Ally was finished helping him stack water glasses, Bethany was gone.

